   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The composite has outer function F with \\( \\frac{d}{du} \\sqrt{u} = \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}} \\) and inner function \\( u = 2 x^{2} + 17 \\), whose derivative is \\( 4 x \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99023",
         "rule_named": "identify the layers"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "By the product rule and the chain rule, \\( h'(x) = \\frac{2 x^{3}}{\\sqrt{2 x^{2} + 17}} + 2 x \\sqrt{2 x^{2} + 17} \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99023",
         "rule_named": "product rule with the chain rule"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "At x = 2 the inner value is 25 and the inner derivative is 8, so \\( h'(2) = 20 + 4 \\cdot \\frac{1}{10} \\cdot 8 = \\frac{116}{5} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
